cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use quickmeasure, please cite it as below."
title: "quickmeasure: tree heights from photos with a reference stick"
abstract: >-
  quickmeasure is a single-file web app for measuring the height of trees, or any
  upright object, in photographs that include a reference stick of known length
  standing against the object. The user marks the bottom of the stick and a known
  mark on it, then the base and top of each tree; the height is the tree's length
  in pixels scaled by the stick's pixels per metre, with an uncertainty from how
  precisely the points were placed. It runs entirely in the browser (photos never
  leave the computer), works offline, and exports heights with their source photo,
  reference and pixel measurements as CSV, plus a session file holding every point.
type: software
